# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Carla Verdi et al. (2021). Thermal transport and phase transitions of zirconia by on-the-fly machine-learned interatomic potentials.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-021-00630-5  arXiv:2109.15002v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2109.15002v1 (sha256 cfd70f241a45f419...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 302 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/verdi2021.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the on-the-fly machine-learned force field for ZrO2
# trained in VASP (592 PBEsol structures of 96 atoms selected from about
# 145,000 MD steps up to 2800 K), with Bayesian-linear-regression and SVD
# variants and their training and test RMSEs (Table 1). Phonon-energy
# errors, structural parameters, phase-transition temperatures and
# thermal conductivities are properties, not energy/force/stress errors.

