###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Only 592 DFT calculations were needed out of almost 145,000 on-the-fly MD
# steps; no timings are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Stress RMSEs given in kbar are converted to GPa. Phonon-energy RMSEs (Table 1: e.g. 1.59, 0.80 and 0.55 meV for cubic, tetragonal and monoclinic with SVD) are phonon properties and are not encoded.
# - VASP-MLFF is a new registry method for the on-the-fly kernel force field of Jinnouchi et al. (introduced in jinnouchi2019, later in the queue); the Gaussian width 0.4 A, lmax = 4 and the 2,048 descriptors have no hyperparameter individual.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/verdi2021.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

